        "source_type": "text",
        "source_sentence": "LCST Measurements. Polymers are first dissolved in deionized water, and then the aqueous solution was diluted to different concentrations. The cloud points ofpolymers in this work are too high to be tested by UV. Therefore, the solutions were heated slowly in an oil bath to certain temperature. The temperature at which the solution begins to change from clear to turbid was recorded.",
